  "worked_solution": "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
